# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules.
#
# `app.json` sets no `web.output`, so Expo Router exports a **single** `index.html` and
# routes client-side. Cloudflare Pages serves files, not routes: it looks for
# `/board/<id>/index.html`, finds nothing, and answers its 404 page. Every deep link the
# app itself emits — a magic-link callback, a push notification's `/board/<id>`, a shared
# URL — is a cold load on a path that has no file, so without this line the only URL that
# works is the one you typed to get here.
#
# 200 rather than 301/302: the browser must keep the original path in `location.pathname`,
# because that path is the route. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to `/` and the
# router would land on the home screen having thrown the destination away.
#
# Verified: `expo export --platform web` copies `public/` into `dist/` verbatim, and says
# nothing about it in its summary — the "Files (2)" line counts only what it generated.
/*  /index.html  200
